ion", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "A", "number": 23, "prompt": "Most patients recover in less than ____", "sourcePage": 135, "group": "Extract 2", "choices": [], "kind": "blank", "answer": {"text": "four/4 months", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "A", "number": 24, "prompt": "Important to keep eye lubricated as condition impacts ____", "sourcePage": 135, "group": "Extract 2", "choices": [], "kind": "blank", "answer": {"text": "Blink reflex", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["80c8682bf67dbedb8664f28899595cee1daa6735e863d461b2db287f95cf88bd"], "answerSources": [], "passages": [], "matchEvidence": "Matching sound verified in three separated windows; excerpt questions restricted to the spoken question range", "referenceRecordingSha256": "128cb4d827df46eb638dfc846d7085c30c2ef63047c7cf01f7f630d520deca0a"}, {"id": "listening-18-B-recording-80c8682bf67d", "label": "Listening Test 18 · Part B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "8adfbf2ba6d50c8acb3e74398f98289363200d8864c467f1e795f6d28757b6ee", "pages": [136, 137], "questions": [{"part": "B", "number": 25, "prompt": "You hear part of a conversation between a junior and senior doctor on how to\n interpret the results of an investigation.\n What does the senior doctor clarify about the results of the investigation?\nA. That the results clearly point to portal hypertension\nB. That the results are not sufficient to come to a definite diagnosis\n yet\nC. That the medical history allows them to rule out cirrhosis", "sourcePage": 136, "group": "Short workplace conversations", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "B", "number": 26, "prompt": "You hear part of a training about smoking cessation counselling.\n The speaker points out that this approach is better than…\nA. One not focused specifically on this behavior\nB. One used by other types of specialties\nC. One focused on patient´s worries and desires", "sourcePage": 136, "group": "Short workplace conversations", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "B", "number": 27, "prompt": "You hear a doctor going over an upcoming procedure with a patient.\n What does the doctor explain to the patient?\nA. When they can insert the implant\nB. How they will insert the implant\nC. Why they will insert the implant", "sourcePage": 136, "group": "Short workplace conversations", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "B", "number": 28, "prompt": "You hear part of a conversation between a nurse and a doctor about a patient’s\n medication.\n What does the nurse point out about the patient’s medication?\nA. He took an analgesic before he was admitted to the hospital.\nB. He depends on his wife to get painkillers from the doctors in the\n hospital.\nC. He is mixing over-the-counter and prescribed medications.", "sourcePage": 136, "group": "Short workplace conversations", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "B", "number": 29, "prompt": "You hear two doctors talking about a patient that one is referring to the other.\n The doctor referring the patient explains that…\nA. The previous diagnosis was made by a doctor at another practice.\nB. The previous diagnosis was made by a specialist in another field.\nC. The previous diagnosis was made by a doctor who is no longer\n working.", "sourcePage": 137, "group": "Short workplace conversations", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "B", "number": 30, "prompt": "You hear a conversation between two ward leaders about administrative\n duties.\n The ward leaders agree that...\nA. Their job responsibilities have changed over time\nB. Their job has become much more difficult over time\nC. Their satisfaction with their job has changed over time", "sourcePage": 137, "group": "Short workplace conversations", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["80c8682bf67dbedb8664f28899595cee1daa6735e863d461b2db287f95cf88bd"], "answerSources": [], "passages": [], "matchEvidence": "Matching sound verified in three separated windows; excerpt questions restricted to the spoken question range", "referenceRecordingSha256": "128cb4d827df46eb638dfc846d7085c30c2ef63047c7cf01f7f630d520deca0a"}, {"id": "listening-18-C-recording-80c8682bf67d", "label": "Listening Test 18 · Part C", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "8adfbf2ba6d50c8acb3e74398f98289363200d8864c467f1e795f6d28757b6ee", "pages": [137, 138, 139], "questions": [{"part": "C", "number": 31, "prompt": "Why does Jessica Stokes say it is important to focus on coconut oil?\nA. Because of all of the benefits it is known to have\nB. Because of the recent interest in it\nC. Because of the findings of other research studies", "sourcePage": 137, "group": "Extract 1", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "C", "number": 32, "prompt": "Jessica Stokes points out that previous studies show...\nA. Consumption of coconut oil likely has no noticeable effect\nB. Consumption of coconut oil likely has a beneficial effect\nC. Consumption of coconut oil likely has a negative effect", "sourcePage": 137, "group": "Extract 1", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "C", "number": 33, "prompt": "What limitation did previous studies have?\nA. The duration of the study\nB. The methods of analysis\nC. The number of total studies", "sourcePage": 138, "group": "Extract 1", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "C", "number": 34, "prompt": "Who was not selected to be part of the study?\nA. People living outside of the country\nB. People with no known medical issues\nC. People living close to one town", "sourcePage": 138, "group": "Extract 1", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"assetPath": "benchmark/files/listening-key-18.pdf", "format": "pdf", "filename": "Printed Benchmark answer key"}, "page": 1}}, {"part": "C", "number": 35, "prompt": "Jessica Stokes says that before the study…\nA. Daily food consumption was evaluated\nB. The amount of exercise was evaluated\nC. The medication history was taken", "sourcePage": 138, "group": "Extract 1", "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answ